Files added to the package on top of the `just install` tree. They are not
installed by upstream's justfile but by its Debian packaging, and are copied
unchanged from pop-os/cosmic-greeter at commit 80e8a104b75a01ab8df52bca7b8bde6dbcdb8133
(the cosmic-greeter submodule of cosmic-epoch tag epoch-1.11.0):

  etc/greetd/cosmic-greeter.toml                 <- cosmic-greeter.toml
  etc/pam.d/cosmic-greeter                       <- debian/cosmic-greeter.pam
  usr/lib/systemd/system/cosmic-greeter.service  <- debian/cosmic-greeter.service
  usr/lib/systemd/system/cosmic-greeter-daemon.service
                                                 <- debian/cosmic-greeter-daemon.service

Neither unit is enabled by the package (upstream enables the daemon on every
boot; here cosmic-greeter.service pulls it in only when the COSMIC login screen
is used). Without the daemon the login screen cannot show per-user avatars,
themes or backgrounds (found by the VM session test of build 10).
make-deb.sh copies everything here except this README.
